{"summary":"This execution packet contains context for the 'muse-readme' task, which aims to update README.md to provide a complete, bilingual (EN + RU) guide explaining what Muse AI connector is, how its architecture functions, and how to install and use it. The task contract sets low risk, strictly limits modifications to README.md, forbids code edits, secrets, and '/Users/' paths, and specifies acceptance checks via an external script (node /tmp/muse-readme/check.mjs) verifying that every musebridge subcommand from its help text is covered, required strings ('wss://hatch.metaaivm.com/v1/noise', '[[done]]', 'maxParallel', '~/.muse-bridge/runtime') are present, and a 'По-русски' section exists.

From .agents/plans/muse-packaging.md, the packaging design allows any BB user to install the 'muse' plugin without terminal interaction. When installed, a self-installing runtime places the CLI and ACP agent in ~/.muse-bridge/runtime/<version>/ with launcher shims in ~/.muse-bridge/bin/, overcoming the BB host constraint where only bundled host.mjs is delivered to hosts. Account credentials (cookies exported at mode 0600) captured via Chrome on one machine are synced across connected hosts through hub RPCs in memory without logging or persistence on the hub. The service architecture connects BB to Muse cloud VMs via a Noise protocol WebSocket (wss://hatch.metaaivm.com/v1/noise), exposing an ACP agent (muse-acp) on stdio that drives chat sessions and emits completion signals such as [[done]].

The current README.md (dated 2026-11-02) is outdated: it instructs users to clone and npm link manually, omits several subcommands (such as accounts import, accounts set, and sync targets), and does not mention the Noise WebSocket endpoint, [[done]], maxParallel concurrency controls, or ~/.muse-bridge/runtime directory structures. The CLI source (bin/musebridge.mjs) defines the canonical command list in its HELP text, including doctor, chats, history, send, approve, accounts list/add/remove/check/refresh/import/set, sync targets add/remove/list, sync, login, and --help, along with flags for transports (api vs browser), timeouts, heading modes, and JSON output.","keyFacts":["The task contract for muse-readme requires updating README.md to describe behavior present in the code without code changes, secrets, or '/Users/' paths (task contract).","Verification checks that README.md lists every musebridge subcommand from help text, includes 'wss://hatch.metaaivm.com/v1/noise', '[[done]]', 'maxParallel', '~/.muse-bridge/runtime', and has a 'По-русски' section (task contract).","BB hosts receive only the bundled host.mjs of a plugin; bin/, bridge/, and node_modules are not shipped to remote hosts (.agents/plans/muse-packaging.md).","The self-installing runtime places versioned files under ~/.muse-bridge/runtime/<version>/ and creates shims in ~/.muse-bridge/bin/ for musebridge and muse-acp (.agents/plans/muse-packaging.md).","Account sign-in occurs in Google Chrome, exporting cookies to ~/.muse-bridge/accounts/<id>/cookies.json with 0600 permissions, which can be synced across machines via the hub (.agents/plans/muse-packaging.md).","The architecture links BB to Muse cloud VMs over a Noise WebSocket at wss://hatch.metaaivm.com/v1/noise, driven by musebridge and the muse-acp ACP agent (.agents/plans/muse-packaging.md).","The existing README.md documents an outdated installation workflow requiring manual git clone, npm install, and npm link (README.md).","State and profiles default to ~/.muse-bridge/, customizable via the MUSE_BRIDGE_HOME environment variable (README.md).","The API transport is the default for communication using cookies, falling back to Chrome when cookies are missing or rejected with HTTP 401/403 (README.md, bin/musebridge.mjs).","Approval cards in Muse chats are automatically answered with 'Always allow' by the connector, except for payment or subscription cards which require manual user action (README.md, bin/musebridge.mjs).","The musebridge HELP text defines 17 commands/subcommands: doctor, chats, history, send, approve, accounts list, accounts add, accounts remove, accounts check, accounts refresh, accounts import, accounts set, sync targets add, sync targets remove, sync targets list, sync, login, plus --help (bin/musebridge.mjs).","Account concurrency can be configured via 'musebridge accounts set <id> --max-parallel <n>' supporting 1 to 50 concurrent chats (bin/musebridge.mjs).","The 'accounts list' command tracks slot utilization, displaying busy slots against maxParallel limits for each account (bin/musebridge.mjs)."],"openQuestions":["Several files referenced in the task contract read_first list (bin/muse-acp.mjs, server.ts, host.ts, muse-protocol.md, muse-agent.md) were omitted from the packet, leaving detailed agent toolsets and Noise WebSocket handshakes unspecified.","The packet does not clarify whether 'accounts export' should be listed in user-facing CLI documentation, as it is in the packaging plan for hub sync but absent from the bin/musebridge.mjs HELP text.","The exact end-user installation command for non-developer BB users (e.g., whether via BB UI or bb plugin install syntax) is not fully established in README.md.","The exact role and formatting expectations of the '[[done]]' completion token in relation to agent output and user chats are not detailed in the provided excerpts."]}
